World Waterpark is a water park located at West Edmonton Mall in Edmonton, Alberta, Canada.  Opened to the public in 1986, it is the world's second-largest indoor water park after the Tropical Islands Resort in Germany.  It has a maximum capacity of 5000 guests, an average air temperature of 31 °C , and contains the world's largest indoor wave pool with a capacity of 12.3 million litres.

An indoor water park is a type of water park that is located inside a building.  An indoor water park has the ability to stay open year-round, as it is not affected by weather conditions.

Wet N Wild is an indoor water park situated in North Shields, Tyne and Wear, England.  It was the United Kingdom's largest indoor water park when opened in 1993, a title subsequently claimed by Sandcastle Waterpark.  The park is situated in the Royal Quays complex, and features numerous slides, a wave machine, and rapids.  It was confirmed Wet N Wild would reopen following a takeover by Moirai Capital Investments;
